  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.2', 'Privileged access rights', 'Technological', 'partial', '["supabase.role_privilege_review", "org.access_review_cadence"]'::jsonb, 'supabase.role_privilege_review (partial): No direct Postgres connection available for this audit (Management API token only). Migration SQL shows no custom Postgres roles/grants defined — access control is implemented at the application layer (users.role, is_orcanos_admin), not verified live against pg_roles. | org.access_review_cadence (pass): A periodic (e.g. quarterly) access review is scheduled for this system''s admin/privileged roles (user attestation, 2026-09-15).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.3', 'Information access restriction', 'Technological', 'partial', '["code.static_authz_review", "supabase.rls_policies", "pentest.idor_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.static_authz_review (partial): Account/tenant scoping enforced by per-endpoint convention (_require_account_member etc.), not a structural guarantee — no DB-level RLS backstop. A new module (fda_510k.py, found during this audit) had an unescaped id-filter IDOR gap; fixed during this audit run. | supabase.rls_policies (partial): No table in the project has Row Level Security enabled. All access is correctly centralized through the backend''s service_role key (valid architecture), but the frontend also ships a live anon key for the same project with no RLS as a defense-in-depth backstop. | pentest.idor_review (pass): Previously fixed cross-tenant IDOR issues (C2-C7, H2-H3) verified still intact. A new unescaped-id-filter IDOR/injection gap was found in the (then-new) 510(k) submissions module during this audit and fixed in the same session (backend/fda_510k.py — dossier_id/submission_id now sanitized with urllib.parse.quote before use in PostgREST filter strings).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.4', 'Access to source code', 'Technological', 'blocked', '["code.source_code_access_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.source_code_access_review (blocked): Requires a review of GitHub org/team membership — not visible from the local checkout.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.5', 'Secure authentication', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.authentication_review", "supabase.auth_config", "pentest.auth_flow_abuse"]'::jsonb, 'code.authentication_review (partial): Hardcoded JWT fallback secret (''dev-secret-change-in-prod'') still present in backend/sessions.py (mitigated only by a separate startup validator, not removed at source). No MFA for any role. No rate limiting/lockout on login or password-reset-adjacent endpoints. | supabase.auth_config (partial): Password minimum length is only 6 characters with no complexity rule or HaveIBeenPwned check; MFA (TOTP) is available but not enforced; no session inactivity timeout configured; CAPTCHA disabled on public signup/login. | pentest.auth_flow_abuse (fail): No rate limiting or lockout after repeated failed login attempts on /auth/local/login or the Orcanos-proxy endpoints (M5, still open). OAuth redirect_uri is not validated server-side against an allowlist (relies solely on the IdP''s own registered-redirect enforcement).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.6', 'Capacity management', 'Technological', 'not_applicable', '[]'::jsonb, 'Not applicable to this system''s architecture.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.7', 'Protection against malware', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.dependency_vuln_scan"]'::jsonb, 'code.dependency_vuln_scan (fail): npm audit found 3 high-severity advisories (ws package, fixes available). Backend requirements.txt has no lockfile and uses floating >= version bounds.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.8', 'Management of technical vulnerabilities', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.dependency_vuln_scan"]'::jsonb, 'code.dependency_vuln_scan (fail): npm audit found 3 high-severity advisories (ws package, fixes available). Backend requirements.txt has no lockfile and uses floating >= version bounds.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.9', 'Configuration management', 'Technological', 'partial', '["code.change_management_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.change_management_review (partial): A defined Cloud Build pipeline exists (not ad hoc), but it does not enforce tests or a frontend build passing before the Cloud Run deploy step runs.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.10', 'Information deletion', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.data_deletion_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.data_deletion_review (fail): delete_user() only removes the master users row — does not cascade to a user''s owned repositories/documents/conversations/usage_logs across accounts, and (unlike delete_account) returns no warning about what isn''t cleaned up.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.11', 'Data masking', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.data_masking_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.data_masking_review (fail): 19+ call sites in backend/api.py return raw exception text (str(e)) directly in HTTP responses — real information-disclosure gap (tracked internally as L1, still open).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.12', 'Data leakage prevention', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.secret_scanning", "code.data_masking_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.secret_scanning (partial): No live secret currently tracked in git, but a real Orcanos credential exposed historically via .env.test and design/compliance/COMPLIANCE_HANDOFF.md remains in git history and has not been rotated. | code.data_masking_review (fail): 19+ call sites in backend/api.py return raw exception text (str(e)) directly in HTTP responses — real information-disclosure gap (tracked internally as L1, still open).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.13', 'Information backup', 'Technological', 'fail', '["supabase.backup_pitr"]'::jsonb, 'supabase.backup_pitr (fail): Daily physical backups run reliably (8-day unbroken history), but Point-In-Time Recovery is disabled — recovery is limited to the most recent daily backup boundary (up to ~24h of potential data loss).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.14', 'Redundancy of information processing facilities', 'Technological', 'fail', '["org.business_continuity"]'::jsonb, 'org.business_continuity (fail): This system''s backup/DR approach is configured but has not actually been tested with a real restore (user attestation, 2026-09-15).', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.15', 'Logging', 'Technological', 'partial', '["code.audit_logging_review", "supabase.audit_logging"]'::jsonb, 'code.audit_logging_review (partial): security_audit_log mechanism implemented and wired into login failures and admin actions, but silently no-ops to stdout if migration 009 hasn''t been applied — not confirmed applied to production from code alone. | supabase.audit_logging (partial): Supabase''s native Postgres/auth audit logging is explicitly disabled on this project (audit_log_disable_postgres=true). The app''s own security_audit_log table exists but no periodic review process or durable off-instance export is confirmed.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.16', 'Monitoring activities', 'Technological', 'partial', '["code.audit_logging_review", "supabase.audit_logging"]'::jsonb, 'code.audit_logging_review (partial): security_audit_log mechanism implemented and wired into login failures and admin actions, but silently no-ops to stdout if migration 009 hasn''t been applied — not confirmed applied to production from code alone. | supabase.audit_logging (partial): Supabase''s native Postgres/auth audit logging is explicitly disabled on this project (audit_log_disable_postgres=true). The app''s own security_audit_log table exists but no periodic review process or durable off-instance export is confirmed.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.17', 'Clock synchronization', 'Technological', 'not_applicable', '[]'::jsonb, 'Not applicable to this system''s architecture.', '2026-09-15'),
