  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.25', 'Secure development life cycle', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.secure_sdlc_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.secure_sdlc_review (fail): No CI pipeline runs tests, build, or a security gate (dependency audit/SAST/secret-scan) before deploy. No GitHub Actions found; cloudbuild.yaml deploys with no test step. No branch protection evidence.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.26', 'Application security requirements', 'Technological', 'partial', '["pentest.ssrf_review", "pentest.injection_review", "pentest.security_headers", "pentest.input_validation"]'::jsonb, 'pentest.injection_review (pass): Previously fixed injection issues (L3, H1 markdown sanitization, C6 iframe sandboxing) verified still in place. The same-session fix to backend/fda_510k.py (see pentest.idor_review) also closes this module''s PostgREST filter-injection surface. | pentest.security_headers (partial): CORS avoids the wildcard-origin + allow_credentials=True combination (credentials hardcoded False), but allow_origins defaults to ''*'' in any deployment where ALLOWED_ORIGINS is unset (M2, tracked as not fully locked down). No CSP or HSTS header is set by the application itself. | pentest.input_validation (partial): Zip-bomb guard (entry count + total size caps) confirmed intact for zip extraction. General document-upload endpoints have no confirmed server-side max-upload-size or file-type check at the API layer.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.27', 'Secure system architecture and engineering principles', 'Technological', 'partial', '["code.static_authz_review", "code.env_separation_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.static_authz_review (partial): Account/tenant scoping enforced by per-endpoint convention (_require_account_member etc.), not a structural guarantee — no DB-level RLS backstop. A new module (fda_510k.py, found during this audit) had an unescaped id-filter IDOR gap; fixed during this audit run. | code.env_separation_review (partial): Dev/test/prod separated by env-file convention, but .env.test previously held a real (not synthetic) Orcanos credential that leaked into git history and has not been rotated.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.28', 'Secure coding', 'Technological', 'fail', '["pentest.injection_review", "code.secure_sdlc_review"]'::jsonb, 'pentest.injection_review (pass): Previously fixed injection issues (L3, H1 markdown sanitization, C6 iframe sandboxing) verified still in place. The same-session fix to backend/fda_510k.py (see pentest.idor_review) also closes this module''s PostgREST filter-injection surface. | code.secure_sdlc_review (fail): No CI pipeline runs tests, build, or a security gate (dependency audit/SAST/secret-scan) before deploy. No GitHub Actions found; cloudbuild.yaml deploys with no test step. No branch protection evidence.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.29', 'Security testing in development and acceptance', 'Technological', 'fail', '["code.dependency_vuln_scan", "pentest.auth_flow_abuse", "pentest.idor_review", "pentest.ssrf_review", "pentest.injection_review"]'::jsonb, 'code.dependency_vuln_scan (fail): npm audit found 3 high-severity advisories (ws package, fixes available). Backend requirements.txt has no lockfile and uses floating >= version bounds. | pentest.auth_flow_abuse (fail): No rate limiting or lockout after repeated failed login attempts on /auth/local/login or the Orcanos-proxy endpoints (M5, still open). OAuth redirect_uri is not validated server-side against an allowlist (relies solely on the IdP''s own registered-redirect enforcement). | pentest.idor_review (pass): Previously fixed cross-tenant IDOR issues (C2-C7, H2-H3) verified still intact. A new unescaped-id-filter IDOR/injection gap was found in the (then-new) 510(k) submissions module during this audit and fixed in the same session (backend/fda_510k.py — dossier_id/submission_id now sanitized with urllib.parse.quote before use in PostgREST filter strings). | pentest.injection_review (pass): Previously fixed injection issues (L3, H1 markdown sanitization, C6 iframe sandboxing) verified still in place. The same-session fix to backend/fda_510k.py (see pentest.idor_review) also closes this module''s PostgREST filter-injection surface.', '2026-09-15'),
  ('orcanos-qms', 'A.8.30', 'Outsourced development', 'Technological', 'partial', '["org.subprocessor_dpa"]'::jsonb, 'org.subprocessor_dpa (partial): Not formally verified. Orcanos (the underlying data platform) holds ISO 27001 certification, which typically includes standard DPA-equivalent terms; Supabase and GCP both offer standard DPAs accepted via their terms of service. No one has explicitly confirmed the signed documents for this system (user attestation, 2026-09-15).', '2026-09-15'),
